\": 1572}, {\"distinct_partners\": 0, \"events\": 0, \"node\": 1781}], \"window\": [22884, 24883]}", "latency_ms": 2, "tokens_before": 31681, "tokens_after": 31681, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_2839846d", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1885, 1460], "window": [13283, 32483], "confidence": 0.82, "narrative": "Both endpoints are low-activity nodes in this window (4 events each, step_02). 1460 has only three in-neighbours: 632, 765, 1045 (step_04), so any influence path must terminate through one of these. 1885's only neighbours are 749, 1132, 1572, 1781 (step_03); in the 2-hop neighbourhood of 1885 (87 nodes, step_03) neither 1460 nor 632/765 appears, and the only bridge toward 1460 is 1885-1132-1045-1460 (1045->1460 confirmed, step_13; 1045's in-neighbours are only 981 and 1682, step_14). Timing kills that route: the 1885-1132 edge does not exist anywhere in [13283, 30083] (step_11, step_12, step_15), i.e. it occurs only in the final bucket [30084, 32483] where 1885's two remaining events fall (step_06), whereas all of 1460's activity ends by ~27683 (step_07, step_09). 1885's earlier events are at ~[17484,18083] and ~[22884,23483] (step_08); the only plausible intermediary active then is 749, which has exactly one event in [22884,24883] (step_16) \u2014 the contact with 1885 itself \u2014 so no onward relay within the 600-unit gap constraint, and 749 has no edge to 632/765/1045 (step_03). 1045 itself has only 2 events in the whole span [15684,27683] (step_10). Hence the static connection exists only through a link that is temporally out of order; there is no time-respecting chain with <=600-unit gaps from 1885 to 1460.", "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_2839846d\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1885, 1460],\n  \"window\": [13283, 32483],\n  \"confidence\": 0.82,\n  \"narrative\": \"Both endpoints are low-activity nodes in this window (4 events each, step_02). 1460 has only three in-neighbours: 632, 765, 1045 (step_04), so any influence path must terminate through one of these. 1885's only neighbours are 749, 1132, 1572, 1781 (step_03); in the 2-hop neighbourhood of 1885 (87 nodes, step_03) neither 1460 nor 632/765 appears, and the only bridge toward 1460 is 1885-1132-1045-1460 (1045->1460 confirmed, step_13; 1045's in-neighbours are only 981 and 1682, step_14). Timing kills that route: the 1885-1132 edge does not exist anywhere in [13283, 30083] (step_11, step_12, step_15), i.e. it occurs only in the final bucket [30084, 32483] where 1885's two remaining events fall (step_06), whereas all of 1460's activity ends by ~27683 (step_07, step_09). 1885's earlier events are at ~[17484,18083] and ~[22884,23483] (step_08); the only plausible intermediary active then is 749, which has exactly one event in [22884,24883] (step_16) \u2014 the contact with 1885 itself \u2014 so no onward relay within the 600-unit gap constraint, and 749 has no edge to 632/765/1045 (step_03). 1045 itself has only 2 events in the whole span [15684,27683] (step_10). Hence the static connection exists only through a link that is temporally out of order; there is no time-respecting chain with <=600-unit gaps from 1885 to 1460.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ]\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 40028, "total_output_tokens": 7677, "total_tokens": 47705, "total_latency_ms": 99801, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}